From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:47:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] The total mode in the operators and the instructions

check_safe takes the SemMode of PR4: in the partial mode, the default
instance, it checks the safety conditions as before; in the total mode it
checks nothing. mk_sem_op and mk_semi inherit the mode, and so do
sem_sop1_typed, sem_sop2_typed, sem_opN_typed, id_semi, semi, sopn_sem_,
sopn_sem, sem_sop1, sem_sop2, sem_opN and exec_sopn: a definition in a
section with a SemMode in context follows that instance, everything else
keeps its meaning. mk_semi keeps the init mask in both modes: the total mode
removes the failures, not the undefined outputs.

mk_sem_op2E is stated for any mode.

No downstream proof changes. The OCaml side is unchanged: no OCaml code
calls exec_sopn or sem_sop*, and the extracted descriptors pass the
instance themselves.

(cherry picked from commit e8482e727ce2dafb1aafcdf2741a9be20df59067)
